.TH BACKUP\-VERIFY 1 "2026-09" "backup-verify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
backup-verify \- prove that your backups restore, on a schedule
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B backup-verify
.B run
.I PLAN
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a plan in YAML, fetches the latest backup, boots a scratch container,
loads the dump, runs smoke checks and tears everything down.
.PP
Exit 0 means the backup is real. Anything else means you found out today,
rather than during an incident.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI run " PLAN"
Run one verification plan end to end.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Keep the scratch container afterwards, for inspection.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The backup restored and passed its smoke checks.
.TP
.B non-zero
It did not.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Verify nightly, from cron:
.PP
.RS
.B backup-verify run plans/postgres.yaml \-\-json
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/backup-verify
.UE
